er, weekly p95 metrics, same-sprint fixes) and willingness to audit individual cases demonstrate accountability that reduces procurement risk, though I\'d need to verify these metrics are actually published before committing budget.", "E2": "SCORE: 0.65\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s specific operational commitments (single ticket owner, weekly p95 metrics, same-day ownership) and willingness to audit individual cases demonstrate accountability that addresses the core concern, but I\'d need to see published resolution stats and case studies proving these fixes actually resolved similar issues before recommending to peers.", "E3": "SCORE: 0.72\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s direct accountability, specific operational fixes (single ticket owner, weekly transparency metrics), and willingness to audit individual cases demonstrates the operational rigor and partnership mindset we require for enterprise integration, though we\'d need to validate these commitments through reference calls and a pilot before committing to co-development.", "D_S07": "SCORE: 0.65\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s response demonstrates operational accountability with specific, measurable commitments (p95 stats, single ticket owners, sprint timeline), which resonates with data-driven professionals, but the lack of historical context on *why* these failures occurred and absence of published baseline metrics before the fix makes it harder to validate whether this is genuine systemic improvement or reactive damage control.", "D_S10": "SCORE: -0.3\\n\\nREASON: CEO\'s response shows accountability which is solid, but the post is about legal/enterprise support issues that don\'t map to my session-based audio workflow, and I\'d need to see actual shipping evidence (not just sprint promises) before trusting an API platform with production-critical work.", "D_E02": "SCORE: 0.35\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s responsiveness and operational transparency are commendable and align with our values, but the post reveals support infrastructu